1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,150
Why do cats obsessively squeeze
into cardboard boxes?

2
00:00:03,878 --> 00:00:06,303
Cats seek confined spaces for
warmth,

3
00:00:06,303 --> 00:00:10,016
and cardboard insulates body heat
far better than cold floors.

4
00:00:10,728 --> 00:00:13,878
Wild ancestors hid in burrows to
escape predators.

5
00:00:14,241 --> 00:00:16,853
That survival instinct never truly
faded.

6
00:00:17,216 --> 00:00:20,116
Even domestic cats crave that
sense of security.

7
00:00:20,842 --> 00:00:23,655
Boxes also provide the perfect
hunting blind.

8
00:00:24,017 --> 00:00:26,430
They can pounce on anything that
wanders near.

9
00:00:26,792 --> 00:00:28,505
It is survival practice,

10
00:00:28,505 --> 00:00:29,692
not just playtime.

11
00:00:30,404 --> 00:00:34,117
When stressed, cats retreat to
small spaces to calm down.

12
00:00:34,479 --> 00:00:38,279
The box becomes their safe zone
and it genuinely reduces anxiety.

13
00:00:39,006 --> 00:00:40,669
Next time you see this behavior,

14
00:00:40,669 --> 00:00:41,431
do not laugh.

15
00:00:41,794 --> 00:00:44,556
That humble box is doing more than
entertaining them;

16
00:00:44,956 --> 00:00:47,344
it is keeping them calm and
confident.

17
00:00:48,064 --> 00:00:50,789
So the next time your cat claims a
delivery box,

18
00:00:50,789 --> 00:00:51,477
leave it be.

19
00:00:51,839 --> 00:00:54,939
Follow along as we decode more
feline behavior.
